# Vigil Multi-Repo Source Control — Colored Tabs Spec

**What this file is:** the **product + UX contract** for Source Control when the user works on **more than one Git repository** at once — inspired by Cursor/VS Code multi-repo SCM, but **better**: **colored titled tabs** instead of a tall stacked list where repo headers get lost.  
**Status:** EXECUTING — **Phase A+B ✅** (colored repo tabs + active-repo git cwd + persist + drafts). In-window project switcher **cancelled** — each workspace is its own Vigil window/instance.  
**Related:**  
- Current SCM UI: `src/components/layout/panels/ScmSidebar.tsx`, `scm-commands.ts`, `GitGraphView.tsx`  
- Git ops: `src/lib/git.ts`, `src/lib/scm-view.ts`, `src/lib/scm-menu.ts`  
- Workspace root today: `explorerStore.openWorkspace` → Tauri `set_workspace_cwd` (single root)  
- Roadmap: `.cursor/rules/00-الخطة-العامة-والأولويات.mdc`  

---

> **عربي:** قصة المنتج للمستخدم

## 0. Why this exists (product story)

1. User often juggles **two (or more) repos** — e.g. `VigilAIAgent` (desktop) + `Vigil-AI-Agent-Web` (web) in one Cursor window.  
2. Cursor/VS Code shows each repo as a **stacked block** under Source Control (Changes → repo A → repo B…).  
3. With many changed files, the **repo title scrolls away** — easy to commit into the wrong project.  
4. Vigil should show **one focused repo at a time**, via **tabs**: each tab = one Git root, with a **strong colored title** so identity never gets lost.  
5. Commit / stage / push / graph / branches always apply to the **active tab’s repo only**.

**Differentiator vs Cursor:** same multi-repo power, **clearer IA** — colored tabs > buried accordion headers.

