## 2. Hard answers (locked for planning)

| Question | Answer |
|----------|--------|
| Stack repos vertically like Cursor? | **No** — use **tabs** with **colored titles** |
| Can one tab show two repos? | **No** — one Git root per tab |
| Do agent tools / Explorer stay single-root for Phase 1? | **Yes by default** — primary workspace root remains the “coding” root; SCM can track **additional** Git roots. Open decision: whether Explorer becomes multi-root later (see §12) |
| Commit into wrong repo? | Hard UI separation: active tab color + repo name always visible above Changes |
| Nested git (submodule / monorepo subfolder)? | Phase 1: discover **top-level** `.git` per opened folder; submodule polish later |
| Switch the whole IDE project from a combo inside one window? | **No — cancelled.** Each workspace opens in a **separate Vigil window / instance**. SCM colored tabs are only extra Git roots *inside* the current window (commits), not a project switcher. |

