## 5. UX / IDE surfaces (dream)

### 5.1 Source Control chrome (must)

```text
┌─ Source Control ─────────────────────────────┐
│ [● VigilAIAgent] [● Vigil-AI-Agent-Web] [+] │  ← colored tabs
│                                              │
│  Branch: 05-Compleate-Phase5    ↻  ⋯         │  ← for ACTIVE tab only
│  [ Commit message… ]              [Commit]   │
│  ── Changes / Graph / Branches ──            │  ← existing inner tabs
│  (file list for active repo only)            │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

- ✅ **Repo tabs row** above commit UI (always visible when SCM sidebar open)  
- ✅ **Color per repo** — stable hash from repo path / id so color doesn’t jump across restarts  
- ✅ Tab label = folder name (or `package.json` / remote name override later)  
- ✅ Dirty indicator on tab (e.g. `•` or count)  
- ✅ `+` to add another Git root; `×` on tab to remove from SCM list (does not delete disk)  
- [ ] Context menu: Reveal in Finder, Copy path, Close, Set as primary workspace (optional)   

### 5.2 Color rules

- Palette of **distinct, high-contrast** hues (avoid purple-default AI look; fit Vigil light/dark tokens).  
- Title text uses the tab color (or left color bar + colored name).  
- Color is identity: same repo → same color next launch.  

### 5.3 Empty / single repo

- One Git root only → still show **one colored tab** (consistent chrome) OR hide tab strip until 2+ (prefer **always show tab** for clarity).  
- Locked preference for planning: **always show the repo tab strip** even for one repo.

